From b2833bea1f2d5dc03fb898eeb86544050a74f418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:01:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] dsv41: TF_DS_FUSED_COMPRESS2 (off by default) runs the
 ratio-2 compressor chain in one kernel - scatterRows x2, the dead memset,
 gatherRows x2 and compress2

Switch: TF_DS_FUSED_COMPRESS2 ("1" or "on"; anything else or unset: off). Read once, at Round.init, the same way TF_DS_COMPRESS_SIDE is read (set alike on both ranks; no fingerprint bit, no switches bit: no frames). At the four ratio-2 KV-source layers the chain

  scatterRows(ckv -> raw_kv[rslot]) + scatterRows(cgate -> raw_score[rslot]) + cuMemsetD8Async(ch.invalid)
  + gatherRows(raw_kv -> kvg, idx gi, 2R rows) + gatherRows(raw_score -> sg) + compress2(kvg, sg -> lat2)

(6 launches a layer, ~24 a round) becomes one tf_ds_compress2x_kernel launch (grid.x = R, one block a group, 256 threads), followed as before by the Triton RMSNorm into rd.lat (outside the fusion, unchanged).

Why bit-identical. The kernel performs the same reads from the same bytes in the same order: (1) phase 1 copies this round's rows ckv[g]/cgate[g] to the ring at rslot[g] - the same bytes scatterRows copies (uint4 when aligned, scalar otherwise); (2) for each partner gi of the group, it reads either the ring row (a partner scattered in a PREVIOUS round - visible, the previous rounds' kernels completed) or, for a partner scattered in THIS round by ANOTHER block of this same launch, the round's own ckv/cgate row r' with rslot[r'] == gi - byte-identical to what the scatter copied, which is what the base path's gather would return. A drafted verify window holds a slot's consecutive rows (1 + held + tokens), so an even/odd pair of the same slot commonly sits in one launch and __syncthreads() does NOT order across blocks; the resolution runs on thread 0 at the top of the block into shared memory (block-uniform, R <= 48 int64 compares; the GI argument is compared against rslot, not pos, because both sides are slot*raw + (x mod raw) and must agree modulo the ring wrap exactly as the ring would). Partners of this round never touch the ring; partners not of this round only touch the ring; no block ever reads this-round ring bytes, so the launch is self-consistent with no grid sync. The compress2 arithmetic is compress2's verbatim, per channel: the pair softmax with the maximum, sum of exp(s - m) from 0 in order, fdiv_rn of expf, the products fmul_rn, and the pair's sum as reduce_kernel's thread_reduce_impl adds it (two used of four accumulators from 0, combined in order), rounded float2bfloat16_rn. The ch.invalid memset is dropped on this path only: the flag is write-only everywhere on it (gatherRows writes 1 on out-of-range; nothing reads it, tree-wide - the flag exists for prompt.zig's fill path, which this patch does not touch); the kernel still writes 1 to it if a partner is out of range (gatherRows parity, still unread), and zero-fills that partner's row instead of leaving the base path's stale kvg/sg bytes - deterministic, and unreachable in this family (gi comes from the same glue as rslot; a match resolves to ckv anyway).

The cross-block race was found in review of the first draft of this patch (single __syncthreads(), partners read the ring directly): on every drafted verify round with an even/odd pair in one window - i.e. effectively all of them - an odd row's partner could be read from the ring before the even row's block wrote it, and odd p rows commit to the real compressed target (only even p writes the scratch), so the bytes would have differed from the base path. Fixed by the rslot resolution above; the review's rejection is worth more than the kernel is.

Both launch paths share the choice: compressorChain (round.zig) selects fused vs unfused at ratio 2 by rd.fused_compress2, so TF_DS_COMPRESS_SIDE's forked chain gets the same treatment as the inline path. The RMSNorm after stays outside and on the same stream/Tri.

Bits: identical (same reads, same order, same arithmetic; the only intentional difference is the dead flag's memset is gone on this path and the unreachable out-of-range partner yields zeros instead of stale bytes). Expected on the pair: exact.py IDENTICAL; the gain, if any, is launch overhead at the 4 ratio-2 layers (~20 launches a round off) - the eager phase profile (tf-dsv41-lanes --profile 2) decides whether that is worth anything; if the gathers and the experts own the round (16/31 ms of 34/56 ms eager), stop here and keep the switch off (but harmless).

.cu compile: none on this host (no nvcc): the new kernel passed a syntax-only check with clang++ against a plain-C++ stub of cuda_runtime/cuda_bf16 (rc 0, no diagnostics); the image's nvcc on the Sparks is the first real compile. Host gates: `zig build test` (one reported spurious "failed command" on this host - the pre-existing flaky KV-shard binary; it and every .zig-cache/o test binary pass standalone, 408/408 in the family suite), and `zig build install native -Dfatbins=/home/colum/.cache/tf-dummy-fatbins` succeeds (the CUDA path type-checks; the .cu itself is not compiled here).

Not run here: any pair, any smoke, exact.py.

